[49m[38;5;10m+     1[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # CONFIGS.md — configuration-surface table (Phase A) / valid-path tests (Phase B)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axes the C code actually branches on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Runtime options.** The public API takes no option struct and no flags; the two
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m things a consumer can configure are environment variables read at call time:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | option | read at | effect |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |--------|---------|--------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `LOG_FILE` | `logger.c:34` | `getenv("LOG_FILE") ? it : "default.log"`, opened with mode `"a"` (append, created if missing). Chooses the sink for *all* log output and, when it fails to open, flips `initialize_logger` to the `-1` path. |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `MAX_TASKS` | `task_manager.c:39` | `getenv("MAX_TASKS") ? atoi(it) : 10` → `manager->max_tasks`, which is both the `add_task` capacity check (`task_manager.c:54`) and the multiplicand of the tasks-array `malloc` (`task_manager.c:42`). Parsed with `atoi`, so it accepts leading whitespace/sign/garbage tails and truncates `long`→`int`. |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There are no `#ifdef`s in `c_src`, and the Rust crate declares no `[features]`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (`translation/Cargo.toml`), so the only feature combination that exists is the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m default one — see `check_all_features.sh`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Entry points.** Ten exported functions, in two layers:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * low level — `initialize_logger`, `log_info`, `log_warning`, `log_error`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `finalize_logger`, `create_task_manager`, `add_task`, `print_tasks`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `destroy_task_manager`;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * one-shot convenience wrapper — `driver`, which composes all nine.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Both layers are driven directly below; rows 1–24 use the low-level API (including
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m hand-built `TaskManager` structs, which reach states the wrapper cannot produce),
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m rows 25–40 drive `driver`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Input shapes the code special-cases.**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `description` length vs the 255-byte `strncpy` bound and the fixed
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `char[256]` field: 0, 1, 2…254, **255**, **256**, **257**, ≫256.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `description` bytes: pure ASCII, bytes ≥ 0x80 (invalid UTF-8 — fatal for any
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `String`-based translation), and `printf` conversion specifiers (`%s`, `%d`,
